 "answer": "**I wouldn’t recommend exercising outdoors in Jakarta today, Saturday, October 17.** It’s forecast to reach about **36°C (96°F)**, with a heat-related dehydration and heatstroke warning. Current air-quality readings also vary by source but are in the **unhealthy to very unhealthy** range. ([iqair.com](https://www.iqair.com/air-quality/indonesia/jakarta))\n\nChoose an indoor workout instead—especially if you have asthma or a heart or lung condition. If you do go outside, keep it brief and easy, avoid the hottest part of the day, and check a nearby air-quality monitor first; readings can vary across the city. ([silika.jakarta.go.id](https://silika.jakarta.go.id/udara/ispu24))",
